The example from #102 and #105: tags changes from a list to a map and no lens
maps it, so the implicit copy would put a list where the tip wants a map. Refused
at compile, in the authoring form's terms, rather than at bind.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	tags: [...string] | null
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
Schema: {
	tags: {
		[string]: string
	}
}

ForwardLens: {
	v0_0: _
	tip: {}
}
-- out/error --
error[E0358]: the ForwardLens of tip would copy v0_0.tags into tags, which does not accept every value of it
 --> tip.thema:7:1
  |
7 | ForwardLens: {
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^
  |
  = note: both v0.0 and tip declare tags, so a lens that does not map it copies it
  = note: tags in tip was list and is now struct
  = note: tags in tip was null and is now struct
  = help: map tags in the ForwardLens: a _match, a computed value, or a constant
